        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Toronto Maple Leafs aren't mourning a season that ended in 8th place with 78 points; they're building a future that starts now. <strong>GM John Chayka's Day 1 free agency activity signals a heavy investment in the next two years</strong>, anchored by the signing of defenseman Emil Andrae to a two-year deal and the entry-level contract of 2026 first-overall pick Gavin McKenna - already set to wear No. 92. McKenna, a 6'1\", 20-year-old right winger from Calgary, posted 51 points in 35 games at Penn State and brings size and grit to the roster. Meanwhile, Ryan Tverberg's one-year, $850K extension adds depth to the forward corps. The Leafs have shed goaltender Joseph Woll and defenseman Simon Benoit in a trade for Andrae and Samuel, reshaping their back end while preserving cap flexibility. <strong>What to watch: how quickly McKenna and Andrae integrate into the system as camp battles begin</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated July 5, 2026"
      },
