      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "Bipolarity defines the Blue Jays' July 4 in Seattle, a day that nearly shattered their season before a single, silent gem salvaged it. <strong>The Jays beat Mariners 2-0</strong>, a shutout victory powered by Dylan Cease's seven-inning, no-run dominance that lowered his ERA to 2.79 and added nine strikeouts to his league-leading 137 tally. Yet just hours earlier, they fell to Mariners 11-0 in a bullpen implosion that left them at 42-47, third in the AL East, and 11.5 games behind the division leader. Vladimir Guerrero Jr. remains the story, turning down an All-Star invite while Cease and Varland head to the game, signaling a team that won't hinge its fate on one man. The swing from humiliation to triumph is the real narrative. <strong>Tonight at 5:00 PM ET, they face Mariners again in Seattle, where Cease must prove shutouts aren't flukes and the Jays can finally climb.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 5, 2026"
      },
