        "label": "What's Going On With the Raptors",
        "body": "The Toronto Raptors have already pivoted from a 46-36 finish that ended their season in the Atlantic Division to a quiet, decisive reshaping of their roster. The most critical move arrived just yesterday: <strong>the team signed 50th overall draft pick Jaden Bradley to a two-way contract</strong>, bringing a Big 12 defensive standout and Big 12 Tournament MVP into their system. Bradley, a 6'3\" guard from Arizona who posted career highs of 13.3 points and 4.4 assists last season, slots into one of the Raptors' two-way spots alongside Chucky Hepburn. With Scotty Quickley finally free to play his style under new forward Leonard, the roster's identity is shifting toward grit and versatility. The front office now watches how Alijah Martin responds to his two-way offer. <strong>What to watch for next is the full two-way roster and early summer camp battles that will define the 2026-27 season</strong>.",
